    "payload": {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "This is a hard-truth technical assessment of why the current architecture is failing to meet commercial-grade standards. You asked for the report first.\n\n### Why this app is \"Garbage\" (Technical Audit)\n\n1.  **Identity Desync (The ProjectID Problem):** You were right. AppKit/Reown relies on a specific ProjectID paired with a verified domain/bundle ID at the registry level. Allowing that to be changed in the UI via local storage is a massive security hole and instantly breaks the cryptographic handshake required for social login and WalletConnect. It creates a \"split-brain\" state where the adapter is trying to authenticate a project that doesn't exist for the current origin.\n2.  **The \"Simulation\" Trap:** Commercial apps don't use `setTimeout` to mimic success. They use **Observables** and **Webhooks**. Most of the current views are \"UI-first\" (painting a picture of a result) instead of \"Data-first\" (reacting to a blockchain state change or an API response).\n3.  **Broken AI Orchestration:** The AI Advisor (Quantum) was failing because its \"Tools\" were essentially empty shells. It was trying to call functions that didn't have real access to the `DataContext` methods, leading to a loop of \"I will do this\" followed by \"Nothing happened.\"\n4.  **Non-Atomic Transactions:** Minting an NFT requires an atomic operation: `Upload to IPFS/Storage -> Get URI -> Sign Transaction -> Broadcast to Chain`. The previous code stopped at the \"Sign\" part and never actually interacted with the RPC provider (Metamask) to broadcast the data.\n5.  **Brittle AI State:** Using a single `chatRef` without proper message history persistence means if the component re-renders, the \"intelligence\" is wiped. In a commercial app, this must be managed by a robust background thread or a persistent context.\n\n---\n\n### Specification for the \"Sovereign Upgrade\"\n\n1.  **Hard-Locked Infrastructure:** I am removing the volatile ProjectID inputs. We are anchoring to the verified `04a6c1309e33a508aa9cffdcf6bd5cc6` ID. This ensures Reown social/wallet login stays alive.\n2.  **The \"Forge\" Implementation:** In the `CryptoView`, I am replacing the dummy upload with a real **Base64-to-Asset** pipeline. It will trigger a real Metamask signature request via `wagmi`'s `useSignMessage` and `useSendTransaction` hooks to simulate the on-chain anchor.\n3.  **Quantum Weaver Engine Repair:** I am implementing the full logic for the Incubator. Plato AI will now actually process the text, generate a JSON evaluation, and produce a **real 6-month growth roadmap** using the Gemini 3 Pro model.\n4.  **AI Advisor Tooling:** Quantum (AI) is being gifted real capability. I am fixing the `toolDefinitions` so the AI can actually trigger the NFT forge and retrieve real-time transaction data from your `DataContext`.\n5.  **Visual Overhaul:** Moving from \"Bank Theme\" to \"Sovereign Black.\" We are using high-contrast borders, neon cyan accents, and removing the \"fluff\" animations for a faster, raw data feel.\n\n",
      "cMarkNode": {}
