\n\n**Reviewing Data Validation**\n\nI'm now focusing on the `weaverState` variable within `DataContext.tsx`. I'll be checking `weaverState`, `ai`, `assets`, and the `useMemo` call. I have to confirm the data types and validation, and verify the model settings.\n\n\n**Verifying Schema Structure**\n\nI'm now focusing on the structure of the `responseSchema` object in `DataContext.tsx`. I'll confirm that the schema adheres to the expected type definitions, including nested objects and arrays. I am verifying that the schema follows the nested structure specified in the coding guidelines, including string and object property types.\n\n\n**Validating API Call**\n\nI am now verifying the `generateContent` API call in `DataContext.tsx`, focusing on the content generation request and `responseSchema`. The `responseSchema` now correctly employs the `Type` enum from `@google/genai` for enhanced type safety and conformity with the SDK, addressing previous concerns.\n\n\n**Validating Mint Protocol**\n\nI'm now focusing on the `mintNFT` function in `DataContext.tsx`. I'll be reviewing the logic and parameters, particularly the use of `signMessageAsync` and the message format, to ensure compliance with the minting protocol and data validation checks. I'm confirming that the message construction and image URL handling within the simulated on-chain signature align with security standards.\n\n\n**Validating Functionality**\n\nI'm now checking the functionality of the `mintNFT` function, paying attention to simulated on-chain signature, and data checks within `DataContext.tsx`. I am ensuring that the image URL handling and message format are consistent with the minting protocol and data checks. The verification confirms compliance with the security standards. I will verify each parameter for consistency.\n\n\n**Validating State Context**\n\nI'm now validating the state variables within `DataContext.tsx` against the coding guidelines. I'm reviewing `addTransaction`, `unlinkAccount`, `addFinancialGoal`, and other functions to ensure their use of types, validation, and data handling meet the required standards. Each state variable is being reviewed.\n\n\n**Verifying Configuration Setup**\n\nI'm now verifying the overall setup, especially imports and configurations, to ensure consistency. I'm focusing on the imports and configurations to ensure everything is set correctly. This includes reviewing `DataContext.tsx` and related files to confirm any remaining inconsistencies, including the comments. The error list remains clean, so everything seems in order. I'm verifying that `vite.config.ts` is compliant.\n\n\n**Confirming Code Consistency**\n\nI'm now spot-checking the rest of the codebase for consistency, paying attention to the `Type` enum usage and ensuring that configurations and state variables across the components follow best practices and coding guidelines. This should cover all files.\n\n\n**Addressing the Context Imports**\n\nI'm now going through the import statements. I've examined `FinancialDemocracyView.tsx` and can confirm the interfaces. I'm focusing on line 14 of `DataContext.tsx` to fix the incorrect import of `Type`, now. I'll make sure there's not another import of `Type`, which I have confirmed is not necessary.\n\n\n**Finalizing the TypeScript Fix**\n\nI'm now applying the fix to `DataContext.tsx`. The code contains the incorrect import of `Type`, so I'm updating it. I've re-reviewed the file and can see that the local `Type` import on line 14 is incorrect. I'm removing it and confirming the use of the correct import from `@google/genai` to resolve the TypeScript error. This completes the fix.\n\n\n**Updating the Response Schema**\n\nI'm now refining the `responseSchema` object in `DataContext.tsx`. My recent update focuses on swapping the string literals like `'OBJECT'` and `'ARRAY'` with the `Type` enum from `@google/genai` for type safety and adherence to guidelines. This includes updating the `items` property within the `ARRAY` type.\n\n\n**Refining the Object Definition**\n\nI'm now implementing the `responseSchema` refactor for improved type safety in `DataContext.tsx`. I've updated the `pitchBusinessPlan` object definition to utilize `Type.OBJECT`, `Type.STRING`, and `Type.ARRAY` from `@google/genai`, replacing the string literals. The schema for 'questions' in the `responseSchema` is updated, too.\n\n\n**Refactoring the Schema Definitions**\n\nI'm now refactoring the schema definitions, swapping all the strings, like `'STRING'`, for `Type.STRING`, as well as `'OBJECT'` and `'ARRAY'` for the appropriate enum entries. I've re-reviewed `DataContext.tsx` and updated the `responseSchema` for `pitchBusinessPlan` and `simulateTestPass`. I'm replacing the string literals with enum values.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Refactor**\n\nI've completed refactoring the schema definitions in `DataContext.tsx`. The `responseSchema` now leverages the `Type` enum from `@google/genai` consistently, replacing all string literals with their corresponding enum values. I've re-reviewed all updated components to ensure full compliance with the updated standards.\n\n\n**Finalizing the Data Context**\n\nI've completed my work on `DataContext.tsx`, addressing all outstanding issues. I've ensured correct imports, including the `Type` enum, and the correct initialization of the GoogleGenAI instance. I've updated the `responseSchema` for maximum type safety. There are no outstanding issues remaining.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Mock Data**\n\nI'm now reviewing the mock data imports and state variable types within `DataContext.tsx`. I see that I need to validate mock data imports for consistency, including MOCK_MARKET_MOVERS, MOCK_FINANCIAL_GOALS, MOCK_PAYMENT_OPERATIONS, and the other mock data objects, for type compliance. I'll make sure each matches the associated type definitions.\n\n\n**Validating State Structures**\n\nI'm now validating the state structures and data types within `DataContext.tsx`. I'll focus on ensuring