      "text": "**Considering Base Integration**\n\nOkay, I'm now exploring the implementation details for \"Pay with Base\" and \"Sign in with Base\" buttons. I've been reviewing the documentation and examples for `@base-org/account` and `@base-org/account-ui`. The key seems to be getting the `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy` (COOP) header right.\n\n\n**Refining Component Placement**\n\nI've decided to place the \"Pay with Base\" button within `SendMoneyView.tsx`, as it logically fits the payment flow. The \"Sign in with Base\" button will integrate into the `Header.tsx` to align with a typical login area. I'm focusing on incorporating the Base Account SDK, specifically the CDN version, as a starting point. I need to handle storing the user's address from the Base sign-in within `DataContext.tsx`. The FinancialDemocracyView.tsx will be where I begin work on the `Sign in` feature.\n\n\n**Implementing Base Demo Features**\n\nI'm now diving into the specifics of the \"Pay with Base\" demo. I'm focusing on incorporating the provided HTML/JS examples for the SDK, specifically `window.createBaseAccountSDK` and `window.base.pay`. I'm working on updating `index.html` with the CDN script for `@base-org/account` and adding `baseUserAddress` state and `payWithBase` function in `DataContext.tsx`. The FinancialDemocracyView.tsx will now contain the demo. The Header.tsx will have sign-in.\n\n\n**Integrating Base Features**\n\nI'm now focusing on integrating the Base features with the provided SDK instructions. I've added the CDN script to `index.html`. I'm starting to integrate \"Sign in with Base\" into `Header.tsx` using the SDK's provider. The \"Pay with Base\" button will be added to `SendMoneyView.tsx`.\n\n\n**Adapting SDK Implementation**\n\nI'm now shifting gears to integrate the Base features, deciding to leverage the React UI package from the CDN through an import map for `@base-org/account` and `@base-org/account-ui/react`. However, after review, I'll stick with the CDN script for the core SDK's `pay` function and WalletConnect for identity. I'm updating `index.html`, `Header.tsx`, `SendMoneyView.tsx`, and `FinancialDemocracyView.tsx` accordingly, and verifying the `vite.config.ts` header. I've also reconfirmed the `ApiError` fix.\n\n\n",
